  "name": "Knicken: zwei Stahlstützen bei 70 % und 130 % der Knicklast",
  "description": "Two identical steel columns (2 m long, 20 mm square, pinned at both ends: a Festlager below, a guide above that lets the top slide vertically) carry a dead load. The Euler load is P_cr = pi^2 E I / L^2 = 6909 N. The left column carries 0.7 P_cr: it only bows a little more than its initial imperfection (2 mm): the bow is magnified by 1 / (1 - P/P_cr) = 3.3. The right one carries 1.3 P_cr: the straight shape is unstable, the column buckles sideways within a fraction of a second and settles in the post-buckled shape of Euler's elastica (about 0.75 m of deflection). The force labels show the compression as a percentage of P_cr. Right-click a Stab to change its cross section: a thicker or an H / I section moves the Euler load (the H buckles about its weak axis).",
